## ⚠ Enforcement asymmetry — which controls bind which lane
*(This is the canonical statement of the PM-portability caveat. The three PreToolUse guards are Claude
Code harness registrations; a non-Claude lane never loads them.)*

| Control | Claude lane | {{OTHER_LANE}} lane | Human by hand |
|---|---|---|---|
| `guard-cross-repo-writes` (writes outside repo blocked) | enforced | **NOT enforced** | ❌ |
| `guard-lane-authoring` (declaration before a code write) | enforced | **NOT enforced** | ❌ |
| `guard-gate-ladder` (surfaces the tier's ladder) | enforced (sensor) | **NOT enforced** | ❌ |
| `.githooks/pre-commit` (declaration at commit) | enforced | **enforced** | **enforced** |

**What binds every lane** is prose (this file + `AGENTS.md` + the required PM-disposition emission)
**plus the harness-agnostic `pre-commit` hook** — the one layer no harness routes around, because all
writers converge at the commit. A reader who assumes the PreToolUse guards are universal trusts a
control that is not running. **FM1:** `core.hooksPath` is local config, not tracked — a fresh clone
with it unset has the pre-commit control silently absent. The kit's `test:kit-controls` suite includes
a test that goes RED when `core.hooksPath` is unset, so an unconfigured clone is loud, not unguarded.

## Tool bindings
- **Cross-family lens / external gate:** {{GATE_TOOLING}} *(if you use the shipped Codex/Gemini
  runners, they need `codex` / `agy` at runtime — see `PORTABILITY.md`; if you gate by hand, say so
  here).*
- **Task-lane declaration — enforcement paths:** declaration `.claude/task-lane.json`; ledger
  `.claude/lane-ledger.jsonl` (gitignored); write-time guard `.claude/hooks/guard-lane-authoring.mjs`,
  commit-time floor `.githooks/pre-commit`. Routes: `in-thread` (with the tier) · `exempt` (with a
  ledgered reason). The retired `lane` route is REFUSED by both controls with an explicit
  `lane-retired` state (doctrine retired at kit v1.4.0, mechanism at v1.5.0 — history:
  `core/README.md` § Provenance). Rules: `core/MULTI_AGENT.md` § Task-lane declaration.
- **Repo-specific families** live in `.claude/kit.config.json` (`executedPathDirs`, `stateDocs`,
  `memoryDir`) — read by `guard-lane-authoring` and `check-doc-size`. A structurally corrupt file
  fails CLOSED in every control that reads one: it blocks a gated write, a **code-bearing** commit
  (a docs-only commit exits before the check), and `doc:size`. A legacy `laneRiskTokens` entry from a
  pre-v1.5 adopt is ignored whatever its shape — no control reads it.

